    "done_when": "A new test, tests/test_out_of_repo_claim_is_not_its_own_conflict.py, dispatches a review-role node whose two write paths lie outside the repository. It uses a temporary config home, and a launcher stub whose pointer names a live pid, so that the claim is honoured. The test asserts that the call returns ok with its run id, and no scope-conflict naming that same run id.\n\nA second case keeps the real conflict visible. A different live run already claims one of those out-of-repository paths, and the dispatch is refused naming that other run.\n\nThe first case fails at the base revision, with that arm logged, and passes at the head.\n\nThe negative control removes the own-run exclusion from the out-of-repository path in a scratch copy, and the first case fails with the mutation on the red log's first line.\n\nThe gate `/home/ITER/mcintos/Code/reckon/.venv/bin/python -m pytest -p no:cacheprovider -q tests/test_out_of_repo_claim_is_not_its_own_conflict.py` exits 0 from the worktree. The test files that cover dispatch scope conflicts show no added failures by id against the base.\n\nThe test neither reads nor writes the real ~/.config/reckon.",
    "estimated_hours": 2.0,
    "goal": "A review dispatch still refuses against its own new run when its write paths lie outside the repository. Measured on 2026-09-28 at 04:43Z: `crew dispatch --role review` with two write paths under ~/.config/reckon/crew/reviews/reckon/ returned `scope-conflict`, and the claimant it named, r-20260928T044354744785-review-of-reflex-keys-on-reviewed-run-and-head, was the very run that call had just launched. The run kept working, but the caller was told the dispatch failed. The same defect was seen earlier as r-20260926T214803125717.\n\nThe in-repository case was repaired by a-launch-is-not-its-own-conflict: the post-launch re-check excludes the call's own run id through `exclude_run_ids` in reckon/crew/dispatch.py. Find the conflict path that out-of-repository write paths take, and make it exclude the call's own run the same way, so that a dispatch never reports its own claim as a conflict.",
